              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "supersymmetry#Minwalla98"} Minwalla 98, section 4.2
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ModuliSpacesOfVacua Moduli space of vacua
          %p
            A speciality of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 4
            SYM is that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            has two “branches” called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coulomb+branch"} Coulomb branch
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+branch"} Higgs branch
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg-Witten+theory"} Seiberg-Witten theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#SeibergWitten94"}> Seiberg-Witten 94
            ). Review includes (
            %a{:href => "#Albertsson03"}> Albertsson 03, section 2.3.4
            ).
          %h3#confinement Confinement
          %p
            While
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            in plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            is still waiting for mathematical formalization and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "confinement#JaffeWitten"} Jaffe-Witten
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#SeibergWitten94"} Seiberg-Witten 94
          %h3#reduction_to__super_yangmills
            Reduction to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 3
            super Yang-Mills
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} dimensional reduction
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 \times S^1
            families of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = 2, D = 4
            SYM theories interpolate to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D4+D%3D3+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=4 D=3 super Yang-Mills theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#SeibergWitten96"} Seiberg-Witten 96
          %h3#ConstructionByCompactificationOf5Branes Construction by compactification of 5-branes
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
            super Yang-Mills theory can be realized as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} compactified
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            (
            %a{:href => "#KlemmLercheMayrVafaWarner96"}> Klemm-Lerche-Mayr-Vafa-Warner 96
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Witten97"} Witten 97
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Gaiotto09"} Gaiotto 09
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            on the M5. This in particular gives a geometric interpretation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg-Witten+duality"} Seiberg-Witten duality
            in 4d in terms of the 6d 5-brane geometry.
          %p
            Specifically the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AGT+correspondence"} AGT correspondence
            expresses this relation in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of the theory and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            on which the 5-brane is compactified. See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AGT+correspondence"} AGT correspondence
            for more on this.
